Third-party code
----------------
src/assets/js/vendor/qrcode.js is QR Code Generator for JavaScript 1.4.4
(https://github.com/kazuhikoarase/qrcode-generator), used to show the QR code
for setting up two-factor login.

Copyright (c) 2009 Kazuhiko Arase
Licensed under the MIT license: http://www.opensource.org/licenses/mit-license.php
The word "QR Code" is a registered trademark of DENSO WAVE INCORPORATED.

src/assets/js/vendor/jxl/ is the JPEG XL codec from jSquash
(https://github.com/jamsinclair/jSquash), built on Google's Squoosh, which runs
libjxl (https://github.com/libjxl/libjxl) as WebAssembly. It turns pictures
attached in the chat into JPEG XL, and shows JPEG XL pictures in browsers that
can't yet.

jSquash: Copyright Jamie Sinclair and the Squoosh authors.
Licensed under the Apache License 2.0, see src/assets/js/vendor/jxl/LICENSE-jSquash.txt
libjxl: Copyright (c) the JPEG XL Project Authors.
Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause license, see src/assets/js/vendor/jxl/LICENSE-libjxl.txt

src/assets/js/vendor/mediabunny/ is Mediabunny
(https://github.com/Vanilagy/mediabunny). It reads videos attached in the chat
and, with the browser's own codecs, turns them into WebM with VP9 before
they're sent.

Copyright (c) 2026-present, Vanilagy and contributors.
Licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, see src/assets/js/vendor/mediabunny/LICENSE-mediabunny.txt

src/assets/minesweeper/ (code, pictures and fonts) is Minesweeper by Nick Arocho
(https://github.com/nickarocho/minesweeper), the Minesweeper game in the Games
section, with some changes for HB Hub: a few small fixes, and the mines are
kept on HB Hub's server, for the leaderboard. No license is stated.
HB Hub isn't associated with Microsoft. Windows is a trademark of Microsoft Corporation.

